{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c50b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9ad-5350-7732-bcf8-b01012a6b1d2"},"sequence":224,"recorded_at":1780531400000443,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0a9ad-dd4e-7ad0-bb50-c69d26d3954c"},"task_id":"01a0a9ad-dd4e-7ad0-bb50-c69d26d3954c","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0a9ad-dd4e-7ad0-bb50-c69d26d3954c","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/r3/r2outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-304bw2 — R2 focused catalog/lifecycle rework (developer outcome)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Revision 2 adopts the four exact rev1 reviewer probes as maintained\n6|production-entry regressions and fixes F1–F4 at the root cause, preserving\n7|accepted registration/global installer lease, corrected real login policy,\n8|and the existing repository editor. No production runner was stopped,\n9|re-registered, or interrupted; the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the\n10|Story worktree for handoff snapshot.\n11|\n12|## Fixes by finding\n13|\n14|### F1 — stopped-only unregister with boundary revalidation\n15|- `Runners+Flow.requireConfirmedStopped` (new): only a positive confirmed\n16|  `.stopped` snapshot authorizes removal. `.running` keeps the stop-first\n17|  refusal; missing observation and every other state (unknown, failed,\n18|  missing, transitional) refuse as unconfirmed. A launchctl permission\n19|  error (`.unknown`) can no longer mint a remove token or reach\n20|  `config.sh remove`.\n21|- Enforced twice: before the remove-token mint and revalidated at the\n22|  `installer.unregister` side-effect boundary (a service started after the\n23|  mint is refused; the unused token simply expires).\n24|- `ManagementWindowContainer.confirmUnregister`: the typed confirmation is\n25|  now reachable only from `.stopped`; other states get an explicit\n26|  \"state unconfirmed\" alert. The flow re-checks regardless (no UI tests).\n27|\n28|### F2 — write-path server/scope/agentID/service binding on Apply\n29|- `Runners+Flow.bindApplyIdentity` (new): re-reads the mutable local\n30|  registration at Apply time and requires server host, org scope, agent ID\n31|  and name to still match, plus the catalog entry to still point at the\n32|  verified canonical directory. A same-path foreign host, scope edit, or\n33|  relink fails instead of writing another server's group.\n34|- `Runners+Flow.sessionStill` (new): the started session (user + server)\n35|  is re-checked after authentication and again at the PUT boundary; a\n36|  logout/account/server switch mid-operation stops silently with no write\n37|  into the changed session (same shape as `refreshRemote`).\n38|\n39|### F3 — collision-safe persistent service identities\n40|- `RunnerCatalogStore.importedServiceLabel` (new): folder imports get\n41|  `actions.runner.imported.<name>-<8 hex canonical-path hash>` —\n42|  deterministic per directory, distinct per path.\n43|- Conflicting labels refuse: `importCandidate` refuses a manifest label\n44|  already owned by another entry, and `catalog.add/update` refuse\n45|  duplicate labels (directory dedupe keeps priority, so the symlink-alias\n46|  error is unchanged).\n47|- Supporting refinement found by the new per-runner-control regression:\n48|  `RunnerControllers.validateManifestMatches` and `references` now compare\n49|  WorkingDirectory/ProgramArguments by canonical identity. The stored path\n50|  and the bookmark-resolved directory can differ in spelling (`/var` vs\n51|  `/private/var`) for the same installation; string comparison broke\n52|  control of imported runners on such paths. Wrong-directory manifests\n53|  still refuse (carryover mutant re-verified).\n54|\n55|### F4 — migration completion independent of count, fail-closed persistence\n56|- `RunnerCatalogStore.File.migrated`: one-time migration seals the catalog\n57|  — including an empty result — and an initialized (even explicitly\n58|  emptied) catalog is authoritative. Removing the last entry never\n59|  resurrects it at restart. Legacy files without the flag seal in place\n60|  without touching entries.\n61|- Checked reads: missing file is first-run absence; malformed/unreadable/\n62|  unsupported-version stores throw (`persistenceUnreadable`,\n63|  `unsupportedVersion`) instead of masquerading as empty. Migration never\n64|  runs on them, and `add/remove/update` never overwrite them. `load()`\n65|  stays a fail-soft display read and is documented as such.\n66|\n67|## Production call sites\n68|\n69|| Fix | Call site |\n70||---|---|\n71|| F1 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.unregister)` → `requireConfirmedStopped` (×2) → `RunnerInstallerService.unregister` |\n72|| F2 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.applyGroupAccess)` → `bindApplyIdentity` (×2) + `sessionStill` (×2) → `GitHubRunnerAPIClient.setGroupRepositories` |\n73|| F3 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.importFolder)` → `importedServiceLabel` → `RunnerCatalogStore.add`; control via `LaunchAgentService.setEnabled` |\n74|| F4 | `Runners.Flow.apply(.loadCatalog)` → `RunnerCatalogStore.migrateIfNeeded`; mutations via `add/remove/update` |\n75|| F1 UI | `ManagementWindowContainer.confirmUnregister` (manual bound, no UI tests) |\n76|\n77|## Tests: 13 new, 210 total green\n78|\n79|Adopted probes (failed exit 1 on rev1, pass now):\n80|`reviewUnknownServiceMustRefuseUnregister`,\n81|`reviewRemovedLastEntryMustStayRemovedOnMigration`,\n82|`reviewSameNameFolderImportsMustHaveDistinctServiceIDs`,\n83|`reviewCrossServerGroupApplyMustRefuse`.\n84|\n85|New bounds: `unregisterRevalidatesStoppedAtSideEffectBoundary` (F1),\n86|`applyGroupAccessStopsWhenSessionChangesMidApply` and\n87|`applyGroupAccessStopsWhenServerSwitchesMidApply` (F2),\n88|`sameNameFolderImportsControlIndependently`,\n89|`importRefusesConflictingManifestLabel`,\n90|`catalogRefusesDuplicateServiceLabel` (F3),\n91|`migrationFailsClosedOnMalformedPersistence`,\n92|`migrationFailsClosedOnUnsupportedVersion`,\n93|`migrationSealsLegacyStoreWithoutTouchingEntries` (F4).\n94|\n95|Updated: `unregisterRemovesRemoteKeepsFilesAndEntry` gains the third\n96|launchd observation (pre-check, boundary revalidation, refresh).\n97|\n98|AC coverage: still 18 of 19 rows driven through production entry points\n99|(row 18 remains the stated manual-UI bound); rows 3/11/12/16 now carry the\n100|negative boundaries the verdict required.\n101|\n102|## Mutant evidence: 8 narrowing + 1 delete-only + 1 carryover, 0 survivors\n103|\n104|Tree reverted after each run; full suite re-run green afterwards.\n105|\n106|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to | Named failing test | Exit |\n107||---|---|---|---|\n108|| `unregister-admits-unknown` | Stopped gate admits `.unknown` (running refusal retained) | `reviewUnknownServiceMustRefuseUnregister` (2 issues); `unregisterRefusesRunningService` still passes | 1 |\n109|| `apply-admits-cross-server` | Bind keeps agent/scope/canonical, drops host check | `reviewCrossServerGroupApplyMustRefuse` (PUT emitted) | 1 |\n110|| `import-uses-name-only-label` | Label drops path hash (sanitization kept) | `reviewSameNameFolderImportsMustHaveDistinctServiceIDs` (count 1) | 1 |\n111|| `migration-admits-initialized-empty` | Migration ignores `migrated`, keys on empty | `reviewRemovedLastEntryMustStayRemovedOnMigration` (entry returns) | 1 |\n112|| `persistence-treats-malformed-as-absent` | Decode failure returns nil (read-failure throw kept) | `migrationFailsClosedOnMalformedPersistence` (4 issues: migrated + clobbered) | 1 |\n113|| `session-admits-server-switch` | Session check keeps userID, drops server | `applyGroupAccessStopsWhenServerSwitchesMidApply` (PUT fired); logout variant still passes | 1 |\n114|| `catalog-admits-duplicate-label` | `add` keeps dir dedupe, drops label check | `catalogRefusesDuplicateServiceLabel`; symlink-dedupe test still passes | 1 |\n115|| `boundary-skips-revalidation` (delete-only, labeled) | Removes second enforcement point | `unregisterRevalidatesStoppedAtSideEffectBoundary` (3 issues) | 1 |\n116|| `manifest-admits-wrong-directory` (carryover) | Canonical gate drops WorkingDirectory | `stopWorksDespiteMissingRunnerStartBlockedOnBadManifest` | 1 |\n117|\n118|No survivors. The delete-only row is existence evidence for the second\n119|enforcement point, not narrowing evidence (narrowing for that gate is M1).\n120|\n121|## Validation (real exit codes)\n122|\n123|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` → exit 0, 210\n124|  tests passed (197 rev1 + 13 R2).\n125|- `python3 -m unittest discover -s Scripts/tests` → exit 0, 62 tests OK\n126|  (release machinery untouched).\n127|- `./Scripts/build.sh` → exit 0, `BUILD SUCCEEDED`;\n128|  `codesign --verify --deep --strict` → exit 0; `1.2.0`,\n129|  `works.relux.runnercontrol`, fresh candidate in `.temp/products/`.\n130|- No configured linter (no SwiftLint config); build shows only\n131|  pre-existing Sendable-closure warnings in untouched view patterns, none\n132|  in changed files.\n133|- Production (read-only): `macbook-iv` service `state = running`, exactly\n134|  one `runsvc.sh` + one `Runner.Listener` per runner (macbook-iv,\n135|  cocoaskills); no `actions.runner.*` in `~/Library/LaunchAgents` (manual\n136|  external login OFF preserved).\n137|\n138|## Stated bounds\n139|\n140|- UI confirmation paths are manual (root CUA on the fresh candidate; no UI\n141|  tests per task). The production Flow gates behind them are covered.\n142|- Concurrent wizard + catalog edits to the same group remain\n143|  last-write-wins (rev1 bound, unchanged).\n144|- `update()`'s duplicate-label check is defense in depth (relink never\n145|  changes labels); narrowing evidence targets `add()` on the import path.\n146|- A remove token minted just before a boundary refusal expires unused;\n147|  the refused side effect is `config.sh remove` (proven installer-idle).","final_result":true}}}
