s agent \\(agentID) for '\\(agentName)'. Refusing to unregister a mismatched registration.\"\n395|                )\n396|            }\n397|            guard confirmation == agentName else {\n398|                throw RunnerRegistration.RegistrationError.confirmationMismatch(\n399|                    \"Type '\\(agentName)' to confirm unregister of agent \\(agentID) in \\(scope.detail).\"\n400|                )\n401|            }\n402|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n403|            // Stopped-only gate: a positive confirmed `.stopped` observation\n404|            // is required before minting the remove token, so unregister\n405|            // cannot interrupt a job — or a service whose state is unknown.\n406|            try await requireConfirmedStopped(entry: entry)\n407|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n408|            let auth = try await currentUserToken()\n409|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n410|            // Server binding: the verified host must equal the authenticated\n411|            // server; a same-path foreign host never authorizes removal here.\n412|            let verifiedHost = URL(string: address)?.host ?? \"\"\n413|            guard RunnerRegistration.OperationIdentity.normalizeServerHost(verifiedHost)\n414|                == RunnerRegistration.OperationIdentity.normalizeServerHost(auth.identity.serverHost) else {\n415|                throw RunnerRegistration.RegistrationError.unverifiedRegistration(\n416|                    \"Local registration points at '\\(verifiedHost)', not the signed-in server \\(auth.identity.serverHost). Refusing cross-server unregister.\"\n417|                )\n418|            }\n419|            let created = try await api.createRemoveToken(config: auth.config, token: auth.token, scope: scope)\n420|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n421|            // A logout, account or server switch during token acquisition\n422|            // invalidates the unstarted side effect; the minted token\n423|            // simply expires unused.\n424|            guard await sessionStill(startedIdentity) else { return }\n425|            // Re-verify after the network: scope/path edits invalidate stale\n426|            // evidence instead of removing a re-targeted registration.\n427|            guard let reread = await installer.readLocalRegistration(directory: directory),\n428|                  reread.agentID == agentID, reread.agentName == agentName,\n429|                  reread.gitHubURL == address else {\n430|                throw RunnerRegistration.RegistrationError.unverifiedRegistration(\n431|                    \"Local registration changed during unregister. Re-verify instead of removing a re-targeted registration.\"\n432|                )\n433|            }\n434|            let currentEntries = await catalog.load()\n435|            guard currentEntries.contains(where: { $0.localID == entry.localID && $0.canonicalPath == canonical }) else {\n436|                throw RunnerRegistration.RegistrationError.unverifiedRegistration(\n437|                    \"Catalog entry changed during unregister. Re-verify instead of removing another entry.\"\n438|                )\n439|            }\n440|            // Revalidate the stopped evidence at the side-effect boundary: a\n441|            // service started (or lost to inspection) after the token mint\n442|            // must not be unregistered.\n443|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n444|            guard await sessionStill(startedIdentity) else { return }\n445|            try await requireConfirmedStopped(entry: entry)\n446|            try await installer.unregister(directory: directory, removeToken: created.token)\n447|            guard !isCatalogStale(gen) else { return }\n448|            // Remote registration is gone; the catalog entry stays so the\n449|            // user can re-register or remove it from the app. Files stay.\n450|    