{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d21b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a9ad-5350-7732-bcf8-b01012a6b1d2"},"sequence":1896,"recorded_at":1780531400003787,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"7dbcf4d4-d16c-4240-8d6f-402893985bdc"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Revision 3 is handed off to review (board `to-review`, checklist 20/20, candidate left uncommitted for snapshot).\n\nWhat changed, all in `Runners+Flow.swift` plus maintained tests:\n\n- **R2-F1 — retarget refused:** `verifiedOrgRunner` now requires the on-disk registration to still match the server host and org scope recorded at import/relink. A same-host scope edit without re-verification fails with a message naming both scopes instead of PUTing to the wrong org. Load and Apply both verify here, so neither can drift between Load and Apply.\n- **R2-F2 — completion ownership:** Apply carries the starting session past the PUT — a logout then refuses the confirmation read and any access publication (the issued PUT is not pretended undoable). The sibling Load path got the same guards, and error completions publish only while the session still holds.\n- **R2-F3 — unregister session bind:** the operation is bound to its initiating session at token acquisition and at the side-effect boundary, while stopped/identity gates stay intact. The body moved into `runUnregister` so every early return still releases the UI \"unregistering\" state — a retry after re-auth proceeds, proven by test.\n\nEvidence: the 3 exact rev2 probes adopted as named regressions plus 3 new bound tests (Load-completion logout, unregister retry release, scope-drift re-verification that PUTs to the new org only). Full suite 216 green (exit 0), release tests 62 OK (exit 0), 4 narrowing mutants each killed at exit 1 with a retained-gate control still passing, 0 survivors, tree grep-verified mutant-free with a green re-run. Signed 1.2.0 candidate built via `Scripts/build.sh` (exit 0, strict verify inside). Production untouched — both runners still running, no LaunchAgents registrations, login OFF preserved.\n\nOutcome attached as `TASK-260916-304bw2_catalog-lifecycle-r3-outcome.md`, with stated bounds (manual-UI row, in-flight read completion, pre-binding entries without recorded scope).","reason":null}}
